        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5gn",
          "text": "What Is the Covenant of Good Faith and Fair Dealing?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5gq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5gp",
          "text": "Like all insurance companies, life insurance providers are legally required to adhere to the “implied covenant of good faith and fair dealing” under contract law. This is a presumption that the parties that are privy to a contract will deal with each other in a way that is fair, honest and in good faith. Insurance bad faith refers to an insurance carrier violating the rights of a policyholder by breaching the covenant of good faith, often in an attempt to save money on the client’s payout.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5gs",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5gr",
          "text": "How Life Insurance Companies Act in Bad Faith",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5gu",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5gt",
          "text": "Life insurance is a contract between a policyholder and an insurance carrier that guarantees a certain amount of money paid to beneficiaries should the policy owner die (death benefits) in exchange for premium payments. Unfortunately, life insurance providers may deal with claimants and beneficiaries unfairly in an attempt to protect their profitability. Examples of life insurance company bad faith include:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5gw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5gv",
          "text": "Wrongfully or unreasonably rejecting a life insurance benefits claim",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5gy",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5gx",
          "text": "Failing to pay benefits according to the terms and limits of the policy",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5h0",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5gz",
          "text": "Misrepresenting the terms and provisions of the policy at the time of purchase",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5h2",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5h1",
          "text": "Failing to properly inform the insured of a pending lapse or provide a grace period",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5h4",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5h3",
          "text": "Unnecessarily delaying the investigation or processing of a life insurance claim",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5h6",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5h5",
          "text": "Refusing to offer a fair or reasonable payout based on the language of the policy",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5h8",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5h7",
          "text": "Insurance companies are for-profit businesses. Despite promises to preserve the interests of clients, on-time premium payments from the policyholder and the covenant of good faith, a life insurance company may put itself first and engage in bad faith practices to protect its profits. In these situations, wronged policyholders can protect themselves by hiring life insurance bad faith attorneys.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5ha",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5h9",
          "text": "How a Denver Life Insurance Bad Faith Lawyer Can Help",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5hc",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5hb",
          "text": "Hiring an attorney to represent you as a victim of life insurance company bad faith can turn your claims experience around. Your lawyer can provide greater peace of mind during this difficult time in your life – explaining and protecting your legal rights while you grieve the loss of your loved one and navigating the confusing life insurance claims process for you.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b5he",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s5hd",
          "text": "Your lawyer can take over communications and negotiations with a life insurer to fight for the benefits to which you are entitled. If you are faced with insurance bad faith tactics, your lawyer can bring a cause of action against the insurer for you to pursue a fair financial recovery. You can trust your attorney to settle your case as quickly, efficiently and effectively as possible.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
